 "info": {
  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official AWS Migration Hub API (2017-05-31). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Progress update streams and migration tasks are stored tracking records: no migration tool, discovery connector, server or application is contacted, no task changes state on its own, and the only state is what NotifyMigrationTaskState stores (NextUpdateSeconds is accepted and not acted on). Created artifacts, discovered resources, source resources, resource attributes, application states and the other official operations return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. ListMigrationTasks is not implemented because its request carries no stream name, so a task cannot be addressed without its stream; tasks are read with DescribeMigrationTask. DeleteProgressUpdateStream also deletes the stream's tasks, as the official operation documents. DryRun is refused instead of being ignored, and the home Region is not checked, so HomeRegionNotSetException is never returned. No official output carries an ARN, so the IAM resource names progressUpdateStream/{name} and progressUpdateStream/{stream}/migrationTask/{task} are the simulator's reading of the authorization reference, not a documented value. Streams are limited to 100 and tasks to 200 per Region as local limits.",
  "title": "AWS Migration Hub (simulator catalog)",
  "version": "2017-05-31"
 },
 "openapi": "3.1.0",
